IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Minimum Wage Act 1983 (New Zealand) — THE NOUNS.
--
-- Every fact the rule modules read, and nothing else: no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Source: ../source/MWA1983.txt (New Zealand Legislation, version 38 as at
-- 20 December 2023, text extracted from the PCO PDF).
--
-- The Act prescribes no figure. The rates are made by Order in Council under
-- ss 4, 4A and 4B (the Minimum Wage Order of each year), so the Order is an
-- input: `Minimum Wage Order` below.

§ `Minimum Wage Act 1983 — the nouns`

§§ `Specified social security benefits (s 4A(6))`

-- s 4A(6) "specified social security benefit means any of the following
-- benefits paid or payable under the Social Security Act 1964 or the Social
-- Security Act 2018". `another payment` is anything not on the list.
DECLARE Benefit IS ONE OF
    `(a) domestic purposes benefit`
    `(b) emergency benefit`
    `(c) independent youth benefit`
    `(d) invalid's benefit`
    `(da) jobseeker support`
    `(e) sickness benefit`
    `(ea) sole parent support`
    `(eb) supported living payment`
    `(f) unemployment benefit`
    `(g) widow's benefit`
    `(h) young parent payment`
    `(i) youth payment`
    `another payment`

-- s 4A(1)(c)(i), (5), (6): the run of benefit payments that ended most
-- recently. The month count is the caller's, and follows s 4A(5): a benefit
-- reduced by a sanction, or suspended, is still "continuously paid"; and
-- s 4A(6): time on a benefit before the age in the Order counts.
DECLARE `Benefit history` HAS
    `benefits paid in the run`                          IS A LIST OF Benefit
    `months paid continuously`                          IS A NUMBER

§§ `The worker (ss 2, 4-4B, 8, 9)`

-- s 9: "This Act shall not apply to—" (a) and (c) are repealed.
DECLARE `Section 9 class` IS ONE OF
    `none of the s 9 classes`
    `(b) an apprentice bound by an indenture of apprenticeship entered into under an Act`
    `(d) an inmate of a charitable institution who does work in or in connection with it` HAS
        `residing on the premises only because employed there`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `(e) an employee to whom the Home and Community Support (Payment for Travel Between Clients) Settlement Act 2016 applies`

-- s 8(3)-(5): a minimum wage exemption permit.
DECLARE Permit HAS
    `rate of wages per hour stated in the permit`       IS A NUMBER
    `comes into force on`                               IS A DATE
    `in force until the end of`                         IS A DATE
    `revoked with effect from`                          IS A MAYBE DATE

-- s 2: "worker has the same meaning as that given to the term employee by
-- section 6 of the Employment Relations Act 2000" — an input.
-- s 4A(6) "continuous employment ... means a continuous period of employment
-- starting on the worker's first day of work; and includes any employment
-- undertaken by the worker before (i) the worker turns 16: (ii) the
-- commencement of the Minimum Wage (Starting-out Wage) Amendment Act 2013".
-- The three dates below are the first day of each such period, on that
-- definition. s 4A(3)(a)(i) is a date test, so the encoding takes dates and
-- works out when the period is completed.
DECLARE Worker HAS
    `an employee under s 6 of the Employment Relations Act 2000`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `age in years`                                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `involved in supervising or training other workers`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed under a contract of service requiring training for qualification`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a class the Order defines for the training rate`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `benefit history`                                                              IS A `Benefit history`
    `first day of continuous employment with any employer`                         IS A DATE
    `first day of continuous employment with any employer since the benefit run`   IS A DATE
    `first day of continuous employment with the current employer`                 IS A DATE
    `s 9 class`                                                                    IS A `Section 9 class`
    `exemption permit`                                                             IS A MAYBE Permit

§§ `The Minimum Wage Order (ss 4, 4A, 4B)`

-- ss 4A(2), 4B(2): a rate "may be prescribed as (a) a monetary amount; or
-- (b) a percentage of the minimum adult rate". s 4(2): the adult rate "must
-- be prescribed as a monetary amount". Rates are per hour here.
DECLARE `Rate form` IS ONE OF
    `a monetary amount per hour` HAS
        `dollars`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `a percentage of the minimum adult rate` HAS
        `per cent`                                      IS A NUMBER

-- s 4A(1)(c)(ii)(A)-(B), (3)(a)(i): "with any employer ... or the worker's
-- current employer (as the case requires)".
DECLARE `Employment counted with` IS ONE OF
    `any employer`
    `the current employer`

-- s 4A(1): a class of workers for a starting-out rate, "defined in the order
-- by reference to the age (or range of ages) of the workers and 1 or more of
-- the following factors". A factor the class does not use is NOTHING / FALSE.
DECLARE `Starting-out class` HAS
    `youngest age in the class`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `oldest age in the class`                                        IS A NUMBER
    `factor (i): months continuously on a specified benefit, at least` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `factor (ii): continuous employment counted with`                IS A MAYBE `Employment counted with`
    `factor (iii): employed under a training contract`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of continuous employment that end the rate`             IS A NUMBER
    `starting-out rate`                                              IS A `Rate form`

DECLARE `Minimum Wage Order` HAS
    `minimum adult rate per hour`                       IS A NUMBER
    `starting-out classes`                              IS A LIST OF `Starting-out class`
    `minimum training rate`                             IS A MAYBE `Rate form`

§§ `The pay period (ss 6, 7)`

-- s 7(2): "time lost ... (a) by reason of the default of the worker; or (b)
-- by reason of the worker's illness or of any accident suffered by the
-- worker". Anything else is `another reason`.
DECLARE `Reason time was lost` IS ONE OF
    `the default of the worker`
    `the worker's illness`
    `an accident suffered by the worker`
    `another reason`

DECLARE `Time lost` HAS
    `hours`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `reason`                                            IS A `Reason time was lost`

-- s 7(1): board or lodging provided by the employer, its cash value "as
-- fixed by or under any Act, determination, or agreement relating to the
-- worker's employment" (NOTHING if not so fixed), and what was deducted.
DECLARE `Board and lodging` HAS
    `board provided by the employer`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `cash value of the board as fixed`                  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `deducted for board`                                IS A NUMBER
    `lodging provided by the employer`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `cash value of the lodging as fixed`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `deducted for lodging`                              IS A NUMBER

-- `hours engaged` counts every hour the worker was engaged to work in the
-- period, including time lost; `hours of travel between clients` matters
-- only for a s 9(e) employee.
DECLARE `Pay period` HAS
    `last day of the period`                            IS A DATE
    `hours engaged`                                     IS A NUMBER
    `time lost`                                         IS A LIST OF `Time lost`
    `hours of travel between clients`                   IS A NUMBER
    `board and lodging`                                 IS A `Board and lodging`
    `wages paid in money`                               IS A NUMBER

-- The whole case the top-level goal is asked about.
DECLARE `Wage case` HAS
    `worker`                                            IS A Worker
    `order`                                             IS A `Minimum Wage Order`
    `period`                                            IS A `Pay period`

§§ `Which rate governs (the answer to Goal 1)`

DECLARE `Rate that governs` IS ONE OF
    `the Act does not apply to the worker (ss 2, 9)`
    `no minimum rate is prescribed for the worker`
    `the rate stated in an exemption permit (s 8(4))` HAS `per hour` IS A NUMBER
    `a starting-out rate (s 4A)`                       HAS `per hour` IS A NUMBER
    `the training rate (s 4B)`                         HAS `per hour` IS A NUMBER
    `the adult rate (s 4)`                             HAS `per hour` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Enforcement (ss 10-11A)`

-- Who brings a claim.
DECLARE Claimant IS ONE OF
    `the worker`
    `a Labour Inspector`
    `the employer`
    `another person`

-- s 11AA(1)-(2): arrears sought from a person who is not the employer.
-- "Involved" is s 142W of the Employment Relations Act 2000 (s 11AA(3)),
-- an input.
DECLARE `Arrears claim against a person involved` HAS
    `the worker is entitled to the wages under this Act`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the wages are unpaid due to non-compliance with this Act`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is involved in the non-compliance`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is the worker's employer`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `prior leave of the Authority or court`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `unpaid wages`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `what the employer is able to pay`                           IS A NUMBER
    `date of the conduct`                                        IS A DATE

-- s 8(1): what the Labour Inspector must be satisfied of.
DECLARE `Permit application` HAS
    `significantly and demonstrably limited by a disability in carrying out the work`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable accommodations considered by the employer and the worker`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable and appropriate to grant the permit`                                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 11B: the hours an employment agreement fixes.
DECLARE `Hours clause` HAS
    `maximum hours a week, exclusive of overtime`       IS A NUMBER
    `the parties agree to more than 40`                 IS A BOOLEAN
